# --------- Miscellaneous ----------
src/backend/worker_e2e/example_run.json
pipeline_compare_out/
# example_request.json was listed here, and that is why it was missing from a fresh clone.
# It is now TRACKED instead: three test modules, README.md and API_SPECIFICATION.md all require
# it, so ignoring it meant the test suite could not pass on a clean checkout. See docs/BASELINE.md.
# (.venv/ is already covered at the top of this file.)

# ---------- Web app (node) ----------
node_modules/
web/dist/
web/*.tsbuildinfo
deploy/.env
deploy/cloudrun/env.sh

# ---------- Local tool configuration ----------
# .claude/settings.json was committed in the initial commit carrying one developer's absolute
# Windows path (C:/Users/<name>/...) as a PreToolUse hook. In a public repository that publishes
# a username, and the hook would fire for every contributor using the same tool and fail, since
# the binary exists on exactly one machine. Local tool settings are local.
.claude/

# ---------- Optional, copyleft, obtained by the user ----------
# s4pred was committed as a submodule POINTER with no .gitmodules entry, so it never resolved:
# `git submodule update --init` answered "no submodule mapping found" and a fresh clone got an
# empty directory. The pointer is gone. s4pred is GPL-3.0 and optional, and making every clone
# pull it is exactly what keeping it optional avoids -- CONTRIBUTING.md has the setup for anyone
# who wants that screen. Ignored so a local copy placed here is never committed by accident.
src/pipeline/s05_physchem_screening/s4pred/
scripts/copy_weights.sh
scripts/run_test_cases.sh
scripts/smoke_test_model_sync.py
scripts/gpu_smoke/local_test_run.json
scripts/smoke/
structure_benchmark_out/
tests/benchmark/
tests/fixtures/